' UI-42's control: v12_viewport.script with every `resize` and `f11` a
' `resize 640x480` instead, run with the same arguments. The window is
' 640 x 480 already, so the step is taken (a step is a frame, as in the
' other script) and nothing is laid out again. Its game lines and its save
' are what v12_viewport's must be: a resize lays the scene out again and
' changes nothing of the game.
press escape             ' Back closes the manual v1.2 opens on a new game's first world map
wait 3
snap map_640
resize 640x480
wait 3
snap map_1280
resize 640x480
wait 3
snap map_full
resize 640x480
wait 3
snap map_back
resize 640x480
wait 3
snap map_200
resize 640x480
wait 3
mapclick 110,122         ' into Paradise Camp
wait 60
resize 640x480
wait 3
snap place_1920
resize 640x480
wait 3
clickon 106              ' the mercenary: his talk
wait 30
snap talk_640
resize 640x480
wait 3
snap talk_1280
resize 640x480
wait 3
esc                      ' the talk closed
wait 5
join                     ' camped here: the place is ours
wait 10
mapclick 177,150         ' the tent
wait 200
snap room_640
resize 640x480
wait 3
snap room_1920
resize 640x480
wait 3
uiclick 168,248          ' the rat trap put down, at the size the script was written for
wait 5
esc
wait 10
press o                  ' Options
wait 5
snap options_640
resize 640x480
wait 3
snap options_1280
resize 640x480
wait 3
snap options_full
resize 640x480
wait 3
press escape             ' Back: the scene closes
wait 5
save
quit
